# Domain move: cavendish.app -> cavendish.space (2026-09-15).
#
# cavendish.app stays registered and stays an alias on this site, so it keeps
# resolving and keeps its place on the certificate. It should not, however, keep
# SERVING — two domains answering 200 with the same pages is duplicate content
# and it leaves every canonical tag pointing somewhere the reader is not.
#
# Path-preserving, so a link to cavendish.app/rooms lands on the same page it
# always did. The force flag (!) is required: every one of these paths exists as
# a real file on the site, and without it Netlify serves the file instead of
# redirecting.
https://cavendish.app/*   https://cavendish.space/:splat   301!
http://cavendish.app/*    https://cavendish.space/:splat   301!

# RFC 9116 says /.well-known/security.txt is the canonical location, but Netlify
# does not publish dot-directories from the publish dir -- a file generated at
# web/.well-known/security.txt 404s. So the generator writes /security.txt and
# this serves it at the canonical path with a 200 rewrite (not a redirect: the
# well-known URL itself must answer).
/.well-known/security.txt   /security.txt   200
